### Added
- **Bounded local Jhol inference example:** `jhol ai infer` runs a manifest-verified `jhol.linear-classifier.v1` model on `jhol-linear-cpu-v1`; the format is Jhol-owned, has explicit artifact/input/class limits, and ships with a repeatability check.
- **C Instant-Lock front door (`jhol-front`):** ~34 KB clang binary from
  `crates/jhol-trampoline/src/trampoline.c` (build.rs). Warm `install`/`ci` is
  two `stat`s then exit — measured at the process-spawn floor (~10 ms vs
  `/usr/bin/true` ~8 ms). `global-install` prefers `jhol-front` over the Rust
  trampoline. L0 uses `.jhol-prebuilt-key` (no sha2 in the front door).

### Changed
- **Skip store relink on zero-HTTP installs:** when packument/tarball harvest
  (or a full local cache) serves the tree with 0 network requests/bytes,
  `relink_store_dependencies` is skipped; store dirs already carry in-store
  links from prior runs. Runtime `require` verified on the harvest fixture.

### Added
- **Paper L0 prebuilt in Rust trampoline:** `jhol-trampoline` (now
  `crates/jhol-trampoline`) short-circuits `install`/`ci` when
  `/tmp/jhol-prebuilt/<sha256(package.json)>-v2/node_modules` exists — symlink
  `node_modules` and exit 0 (GRM Instant Lock / holographic whole-tree reuse).
  `write_prebuilt_cache` defaults **on** with hardlink-only `cp -al` (opt out
  `JHOL_PREBUILT=0`; no full `cp -r` fallback).
- **Warm install trampoline (`jhol-trampoline`):** thin Rust binary installed as `jhol`
  next to `jhol-bin`. On `install`/`ci` with no package operands, if
  `node_modules/.jhol-ok` is fresh vs `package.json`, exits 0 without loading the full CLI.
- **Lockfile-layout harvest classify:** integrity hits in the login-home /
  `JHOL_HARVEST_CACHES` unpacked store are symlinked into the project cache and
  treated as cache hits (skip download worker pool) — the cold 2× lever.
- **`.jhol-ok` install marker** written with status/fingerprint so the trampoline can
  short-circuit without hashing.

