### Fixed
- **Zero-hash capsule entries:** tree writer resolves tarball content hashes from store /
  session / harvest so capsules are usable for warm materialization.
- **Packument harvest before TTL/network:** empty `JHOL_CACHE_DIR` can still reuse the
  login-home packument cache (0 HTTP on seeded machines).
- **Install markers written synchronously** so warm status survives process exit.
- **Lockfile integrity/resolved under clonefile materialization:** `read_all_installed_packages`
  now looks up `store_index[name@version]` when `node_modules/<pkg>` is a real directory
  (APFS clonefile / copy), not only when it is a symlink into `store_unpacked`. Nested
  inserts also fill integrity from the store tarball. Written lockfiles again carry npm SRI
  + resolved URLs, which unlocks harvest (`sha512` → npm `_cacache`) on the next cold install.
- **Cold-start store preseed no longer rewrites `store_index.json`:** `preseed_store_index`
  warms the in-memory binary/bundled indexes only. Download lookups use `store_or_binary_hash`
  (store index → binary-packages index → bundled hashes). Opt back into a stamped merge with
  `JHOL_PRESEED_MERGE=1`.

