### Fixed
- **A plain `jhol install` could abort mid-materialization and leave `node_modules` unusable.** The
  lockfile-layout extract copied files straight onto leftover destinations from an earlier failed run
  and aborted on `File exists (os error 17)` (`eslint-visitor-keys@3.4.3` reproduced it). Extraction is
  now idempotent: both copy sites in `selective_extract` remove an existing destination derived from the
  same source before copying, so a partially-installed tree can always be completed.
- **The store index can drift from the store.** Entries whose tarball no longer exists (files removed
  by pruning or by hand while the index kept the entry) made installs skip the download and then abort
  at link time, while a fresh cache worked — and a stale entry was verified pointing at a tarball that
  did not exist. The index now self-heals on load: stale entries are dropped once per process and the
  repair is written back (measured: 187 of 681 entries stale, now 0).

