### Changed
- **Thread budgets are now bounded by machine size.** The shared IO pool was a hard-coded 64 threads
  (`pool.rs`) and network concurrency was `cores x 4` (40 on a 10-core laptop), so a single install could
  spawn well over 100 threads and several concurrent installs oversubscribed a small machine — installs
  that could not finish and, in the worst case, a machine that crashed. The IO pool is now `4 x cores`
  clamped to `2..=32`, and network concurrency is `2 x cores` (capped at 16) on machines with 8 cores or
  fewer, keeping the generous latency-hiding window only on larger machines (`http_client.rs`).
  Verified: cold installs of a 3-dependency project complete in 0.04-0.45 s with load staying under 10.
